		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=2325#p2325"><![CDATA[
I'm working on a simulator where you can push a boxcar on rails, problem is I want two p2p constraints to effect the actual boxcar (Dynamic object,) much like an actual train car. So what I did was rooted two p2p wheelbases to the bottom of the boxcar, but just one wheelbase "pivots." The lead wheelbase just acts stationary.   <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_question.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":?:" title="Question"> Is there a law with bullet physics that limits one p2p constraint to one dynamic object? Thank you for any responses.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1140">Rizzo</a> — Fri Nov 03, 2006 4:45 pm</p><hr />
